The official theology was that of strict Yahwism, where no allowances were made for Baalism; 
and no compromises were accepted. The Rechabites (see Jer. 35:1-17) were an example of 
those who would not compromise at all on their strict obedience to Yahwism.

(Note that, there was no theological compromise for Paul in so doing especially since the 
offering involved would not seem to him to conflict with the self-offering of Jesus as a sacrifice 
for sin.)

Attempts have been made to identify the lion as Nero, the devil, and literal wild animals in 
the Roman Coliseum. Others also think Paul is drawing on a biblical image (cf. Ps. 22:21; 
Dan. 6:22).

No condemnation now I dread; 
Jesus and all in him is mine! 
Alive in him, my living Head,

O thou who camest from above 
The pure celestial fire to impart; 
Kindle aflame of sacred love

We sing thine arm unshortened, 
Brought through our sore temptation; 
With heart and voice
